//
// Testplan for TestRIG: QuickCheckVEngine drives the ibex UVM testbench over DII, and the in-bench
// scoreboard compares every retired instruction against a Sail reference model -- CHERIoT-Sail for
// the cheriot flavour, RISC-V Sail for riscv. Same testbench on Xcelium and Verilator.
//
// dvsim testplan format (ibex/vendor/lowrisc_ip/util/dvsim/Testplan.py). The flow is run by the
// root Makefile (testrig-*-xlm / testrig-*-vlt); this file maps the closure obligations in
// ibex_cheriot_verification_spec.md ("TestRIG is closed when ...") to runs. make testplan-testrig
// reports against it.
//
// Test names: testrig_<flavour> for a clean run, testrig_<flavour>_corrupt_<field> for a
// scoreboard fault-injection run (+dii_sb_corrupt=<n> +dii_sb_corrupt_field=<field>). Each run
// keeps ibex/dv/testrig/<sim>_testrig_out/results/<name>.{run.log,result}.
// Tags are the simulators a test must pass on for the report (testrig_results.py counts one run
// per tag). Only xlm (Xcelium) is graded; Verilator runs (testrig-*-vlt) are kept but not counted.
{
  name: "testrig"

  testpoints: [
    {
      name: cheriot_vs_cheriot_sail
      desc: '''**Goal**: every instruction the core retires in CHERIoT mode matches CHERIoT-Sail.

            **Stimulus**: QuickCheckVEngine, architecture rv32emcZifencei_Xcheriot, at full size
            (N = 100 per generator), interrupt and unstructured generators excluded
            (make testrig-cheriot-xlm, make testrig-cheriot-vlt).

            **Check**: the run passes -- no scoreboard mismatch, UVM_ERROR, UVM_FATAL, SVA failure
            or $fatal, and QuickCheckVEngine finished -- and the scoreboard compared a non-zero
            number of instructions with 0 mismatches. A pipeclean or N < 100 run does not count.'''
      stage: V2
      tags: ["xlm"]
      tests: ["testrig_cheriot"]
    }
    {
      name: riscv_vs_riscv_sail
      desc: '''**Goal**: every instruction the core retires in plain RISC-V mode matches RISC-V
            Sail.

            **Stimulus**: QuickCheckVEngine, architecture rv32emcZifencei, at full size
            (make testrig-riscv-xlm, make testrig-riscv-vlt).

            **Check**: as cheriot_vs_cheriot_sail.'''
      stage: V2
      tags: ["xlm"]
      tests: ["testrig_riscv"]
    }
    {
      name: scoreboard_fault_injection
      desc: '''**Goal**: each scoreboard check can fail -- a green TestRIG run is evidence only once
            the check behind it has been seen to go red.

            **Stimulus**: one run per field (rd, pc, trap, mem) per flavour per simulator, with
            the scoreboard corrupting the RTL side of one retired instruction
            (+dii_sb_corrupt=<n> +dii_sb_corrupt_field=<field>; make testrig-fault-injection-xlm,
            make testrig-fault-injection-vlt).

            **Check** (spec "Scoreboard Fault Injection"): the run fails; the
            "+dii_sb_corrupt: corrupted <field>" line is present; the corrupted instruction is the
            first mismatch, at the same PC; there is no "never applied" error. Each run's log is
            kept. Repeated after any change to the scoreboard, the DPI bridges or a reference
            model. The mem and wtag fields need a non-trapping store, which the cheriot stream
            produces rarely, so they are injected at the first eligible instruction. insn
            corrupts the reported instruction (checked against the injected word); rdtag and
            wtag, CHERIoT only, a capability tag on an integer write and on a capability store.
            intr flips rvfi_intr of a retirement that neither traps nor follows a trap: an
            interrupt entry the model did not take, which the interrupt check must report
            (it runs in every stream, so the default generator is enough).'''
      stage: V2
      tags: ["xlm"]
      tests: ["testrig_cheriot_corrupt_rd", "testrig_cheriot_corrupt_pc",
              "testrig_cheriot_corrupt_trap", "testrig_cheriot_corrupt_mem",
              "testrig_cheriot_corrupt_insn", "testrig_cheriot_corrupt_rdtag",
              "testrig_cheriot_corrupt_wtag", "testrig_cheriot_corrupt_intr",
              "testrig_riscv_corrupt_rd", "testrig_riscv_corrupt_pc",
              "testrig_riscv_corrupt_trap", "testrig_riscv_corrupt_mem",
              "testrig_riscv_corrupt_insn", "testrig_riscv_corrupt_intr"]
    }
    {
      name: interrupts_and_unstructured
      desc: '''**Goal**: the core's interrupt entry, and arbitrary instruction words, match the
            reference model.

            **Stimulus**: QuickCheckVEngine's interrupt and unstructured generators, without the
            -x interrupt|unstructured exclusion, in both flavours.

            **Check**: as cheriot_vs_cheriot_sail. unstructured sends arbitrary words, including
            ones naming x16-x31, which the RV32E-register CHERIoT mode rejects, so the scoreboard
            and the reference model must agree on those as illegal instructions. For interrupt,
            the scoreboard gives the model the stimulus's pending bits and requires the core to
            take an interrupt exactly where the model does (spec "INTR handling"): taking one
            the model has not enabled, and executing an instruction while the model would take
            one, are both mismatches. Each is a Known TestRIG Limitation until these tests pass,
            or until the layer that covers the behaviour instead is named.'''
      stage: V3
      tags: ["xlm"]
      tests: ["testrig_cheriot_interrupt", "testrig_riscv_interrupt",
              "testrig_cheriot_unstructured", "testrig_riscv_unstructured"]
    }
  ]
}
